# Build output. `.cargo/config.toml` puts the workspace's build directory at
# `Target`, and the anchored entry is the one that matters: a bare `Target/`
# would match that directory name at any depth.
/Target/

# Turbo's run cache, if a pipeline is ever added to `turbo.json`.
.turbo/

# Dependencies. Unanchored on purpose: the workspace root and every package can
# hold one.
node_modules/

# The resolution artefact. Committed on purpose: the release builds with
# `--locked`, so the same tag has to produce the same bytes, and `--locked`
# needs the lock file in the tree. Updating dependencies is then a commit of its
# own rather than a silent difference between two builds of one tag.
#
# Negated explicitly rather than left unmentioned: a global ignore file for every
# repository under `~/Developer` lists `Cargo.lock`, and a rule that is merely
# absent here inherits that global answer. This line is the one that decides.
!Cargo.lock

# Scratch: probes and throwaway trees. The archive of everything this workspace
# worked from is tracked - `.hermes/research/`, `.hermes/bundle/` and
# `.hermes/tools/` are the record and the tooling - and only the scratch inside
# it is not.
!.hermes
.hermes/tmp/

# Local secrets: any API key, any token. A credential in this repository deserves
# a rule that travels with the repository rather than one that depends on a
# machine's global ignore.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Operating-system droppings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/

# The agent instruction file is source, not scratch: a global ignore for
# `AGENTS.md` must not take it out of this tree.
!AGENTS.md
